  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` and `cargo xtask gate heavy` now check the base branch.\n- The check compares the local `<base>` with `upstream/<base>` and `origin/<base>`.\n- For each remote copy that has commits the local branch lacks, the gate prints one warning line.\n- The line gives the count of commits and the `--base` value to use.\n- The gate plan does not change. The check only warns.\n- The check uses the refs of the last `git fetch`. It does not fetch.\n- New module `xtask/src/stale_base.rs`. One call in `changed_since` in `xtask/src/main.rs`. Quick and heavy share that function.\n\nExample from this worktree, with the default base `main`:\n\n```\nwarning: the local 'main' is 2230 commits behind 'upstream/main' (as of the last fetch): the diff can hold files that this branch did not change. Use --base upstream/main after git fetch.\nwarning: the local 'main' is 1002 commits behind 'origin/main' (as of the last fetch): the diff can hold files that this branch did not change. Use --base origin/main after git fetch.\nchanged since main (f2d78f3): 3265 file(s)\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nWorktree agents do not pull in the main checkout (#1201). Thus the local `main` can be far behind. The gate diffed against it with no message. The diff held many files that the branch did not change, and quick fell back to batch.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins (in `xtask/src/stale_base_tests.rs`, a throw-away repository with fake remote refs):\n  - `stale_base_tests::gate_warns_when_local_main_is_behind_origin`\n  - `stale_base_tests::stale_base_warning_text_counts_commits`\n- Red before the fix: yes. With the old behaviour (no warning), the main pin fails: `assertion left == right failed: only origin/main is ahead: []`.\n- Mutations, each run against the pins, then restored:\n  - No warning (the old behaviour): red.\n  - Reversed range (`theirs..local`): red.\n  - Warn at zero (`behind >= 0`): red (both pins).\n  - Restored code: green.\n- Quick gate on the final head: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` gives 1 step, `xtask unit tests`, ok in 154 s, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes `watchdog_tests::a_silent_step_is_killed_as_a_tree_and_named`, which passes outside the sandbox.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: one error, in `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67` (`clippy::needless_bool`). This PR does not touch that file. The error is on upstream/main on macOS, where the `#[cfg(windows)]` block is compiled out. No clippy finding is in the files of this PR.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The change is in `xtask/` only. No post, toolpath or catalog code changed, so the catalog suites and the heavy lanes do not apply.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real `git fetch`. The test sets the remote refs with `git update-ref`.\n- Windows and Linux. The check uses only `git rev-list --count`, so it has no platform code.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `xtask/src/`.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: The quick and heavy gates warn when the local base branch is behind `upstream` or `origin`.\n\nFixes #3739\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
